    "done_when": "Done when tests/test_the_lane_rate_read_decodes_only_its_window.py , on a temporary ledger holding 2,000 promoted rows completed more than 8 days before the test's clock and 30 completed within the window across two lanes, first builds the ledger's on-disk index (as the live ledger has one), then calls _lane_reference_rates once for a new bucket. A recording stand-in counts the payload records decoded from row sources during that call, and the test asserts at most 60 and that the returned rates equal the base revision's for the same ledger. An all_debug job measures the live reckon ledger at head: the call's peak RSS and seconds are written to a log under the run directory beside the same figures at base. Negative control: at the base revision the stand-in counts 2,030 decoded rows. The test files importing the changed modules add no failure against base in matched arms run as an all_debug partition job, submitted with env -u SLURM_JOB_ID -u SLURM_JOBID sbatch and never on the fleet node. Each arm's log sits under the run directory, opens with its revision and literal command, and ends in EXIT= . The gate command is relative and literal ( PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q <test file> ), and names no worktree path. ruff check and ruff format --check add no finding on the staged paths.",
